PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a solid consensus that F (None of the above is correct) is the only valid answer. The data collectively delineate a physiological pathway during pregnancy where transposable element reverse transcription activates innate cytosolic DNA sensing via STING and downstream Type I interferon (IFNAR1) signaling to expand hematopoiesis. Every specific option (A–E, G, H) incorporates an unsupported or biologically contradicted assertion, such as denying interferon's role, asserting untested insertional mechanisms, claiming lack of immune involvement, or making an unfounded therapeutic leap regarding anemia treatment. Consequently, F remains the only logically and scientifically accurate choice.
}

